\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Zero-mean integer spectrum of the line-incidence operator $L_n = A_n^\top A_n$ and the $4\times 4$ balanced impostor square $S_{\mathrm  {low}}$.} \textbf  {(a)} Comparison of the unprojected eigenvalues $\lambda (L_n)$ on $\mathbb  {R}^{n^2}$ (hollow orange diamonds connected by dashed theoretical branch guides) against the zero-mean restricted spectrum $\mu (\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle L$}\mathaccent "0365{L}_n|_{\mathbf  {1}^\perp })$ (filled navy circles for $\mu > 0$; green circles for the magic kernel $\mu = 0$) across orders $n=3\dots  8$. Restricting $L_n$ to the zero-mean hyperplane $\mathbf  {1}^\perp $ projects out the uniform mode, eliminating the irrational eigenvalue pair $\lambda _\pm (n)$ (reported in \Cref  {tab:spectral_census}) and rationalizing the spectrum to exact integers $\{0^{[n^2-2n-1]}, (n-2)^{[1]}, n^{[2n-1]}\}$ for even $n$ and $\{0^{[n^2-2n-1]}, (n-1)^{[2]}, n^{[2n-2]}\}$ for odd $n$. The mean eigenvalue on $\mathbf  {1}^\perp $ is universally $\bar  {\mu }(\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle L$}\mathaccent "0365{L}_n) = 2$ (purple dashed line), yielding random-shuffle expectation $\mathbb  {E}[\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}(S)] = 2\|\mathbf  {z}\|^2 = \frac  {2}{3}n^2(n^4-1)$. \textbf  {(b)} Explicit $4\times 4$ counterexample $S_{\mathrm  {low}}$ (\Cref  {rem:low_mode_insufficiency}) from \texttt  {energy-decomposition.html}. The configuration satisfies perfect linear tilt balance $\langle X,Z\rangle = \langle Y,Z\rangle = 0$ ($E_{\mathrm  {low}} = 0$) and balanced main/anti-diagonals ($R_{D_\pm } = 0$, $\Sigma = 34$, golden dashed guides), but harbors alternating quadratic and cubic row residuals $R_r = (-12, +8, +20, -16)$ ($\Sigma _{\mathrm  {row}} = 28, 38, 44, 26$) and column residuals $R_c = (+6, -18, +18, -6)$ ($\Sigma _{\mathrm  {col}} = 37, 25, 43, 31$), producing severe line frustration $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}(S_{\mathrm  {low}}) = 1{,}584 > 0$.}}{7}{figure.17}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spectral}{{1}{7}{\textbf {Zero-mean integer spectrum of the line-incidence operator $L_n = A_n^\top A_n$ and the $4\times 4$ balanced impostor square $S_{\mathrm {low}}$.} \textbf {(a)} Comparison of the unprojected eigenvalues $\lambda (L_n)$ on $\R ^{n^2}$ (hollow orange diamonds connected by dashed theoretical branch guides) against the zero-mean restricted spectrum $\mu (\Ltilde _n|_{\mathbf {1}^\perp })$ (filled navy circles for $\mu > 0$; green circles for the magic kernel $\mu = 0$) across orders $n=3\dots 8$. Restricting $L_n$ to the zero-mean hyperplane $\mathbf {1}^\perp $ projects out the uniform mode, eliminating the irrational eigenvalue pair $\lambda _\pm (n)$ (reported in \Cref {tab:spectral_census}) and rationalizing the spectrum to exact integers $\{0^{[n^2-2n-1]}, (n-2)^{[1]}, n^{[2n-1]}\}$ for even $n$ and $\{0^{[n^2-2n-1]}, (n-1)^{[2]}, n^{[2n-2]}\}$ for odd $n$. The mean eigenvalue on $\mathbf {1}^\perp $ is universally $\bar {\mu }(\Ltilde _n) = 2$ (purple dashed line), yielding random-shuffle expectation $\mathbb {E}[\Hline (S)] = 2\|\mathbf {z}\|^2 = \frac {2}{3}n^2(n^4-1)$. \textbf {(b)} Explicit $4\times 4$ counterexample $S_{\mathrm {low}}$ (\Cref {rem:low_mode_insufficiency}) from \texttt {energy-decomposition.html}. The configuration satisfies perfect linear tilt balance $\langle X,Z\rangle = \langle Y,Z\rangle = 0$ ($E_{\mathrm {low}} = 0$) and balanced main/anti-diagonals ($R_{D_\pm } = 0$, $\Sigma = 34$, golden dashed guides), but harbors alternating quadratic and cubic row residuals $R_r = (-12, +8, +20, -16)$ ($\Sigma _{\mathrm {row}} = 28, 38, 44, 26$) and column residuals $R_c = (+6, -18, +18, -6)$ ($\Sigma _{\mathrm {col}} = 37, 25, 43, 31$), producing severe line frustration $\Hline (S_{\mathrm {low}}) = 1{,}584 > 0$}{figure.17}{}}
