\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Multiscale sliding-window Shannon entropy, $2\times 2$ quartet energy census, and extreme board textures.} \textbf  {(a)} Normalized $\ell _1$ window entropy $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle H$}\mathaccent "0365{H}_1(k)$ versus relative scale $k/n$ across five constructive magic-square families ($n=3$ Lo Shu, $n=4,8$ Doubly-Even, $n=5$ Siamese, and $n=6$ Conway LUX). Dotted vertical drop lines connect $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle H$}\mathaccent "0365{H}_1(2)$ to hollow markers representing the $\ell _2$ window entropy $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle H$}\mathaccent "0365{H}_2(2)$ at $k=2$, which drops sharply to $0.91498$ ($n=4$) and $0.90598$ ($n=8$) due to extreme corner/center magnitude clustering in doubly-even diagonal masks, while odd-order Siamese squares retain high local uniformity ($\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle H$}\mathaccent "0365{H}_2(2) \ge 0.94254$). \textbf  {(b)} Joint census of interior $2\times 2$ quartet energy $W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm  {int}}(S)$ and window entropy $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle H$}\mathaccent "0365{H}_1(2)$ across all $880$ Fr\'enicle order-$4$ magic squares. In accordance with \Cref  {lem:quartet_equivalence}, vanishing of interior quartet energy forces vanishing of toroidal quartet energy ($W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm  {int}} = W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm  {tor}} = 0$, vertical dashed line), uniquely isolating the $48$ panmagic squares of Dudeney Group~I. Extremal boards are highlighted: global maximum entropy Square~\texttt  {\#123} ($\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle H$}\mathaccent "0365{H}_1(2)=0.99967$, $W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm  {int}}=512$, $W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm  {tor}}=1{,}024$, magenta star) and global minimum entropy Square~\texttt  {\#599} ($\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle H$}\mathaccent "0365{H}_1(2)=0.94035$, $W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm  {int}}=512$, $W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm  {tor}}=1{,}024$, dark red triangle), whereas global interior quartet extrema across the census are realized by Square~\texttt  {\#145} ($W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm  {int}}=384$) and Square~\texttt  {\#219} ($W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm  {int}}=2{,}816$). \textbf  {(c1, c2)} Texture heatmaps of $|Z_{ij}|$ for the extremal squares. Square~\texttt  {\#123} exhibits perfectly balanced $2\times 2$ $\ell _1$ weights ($w_1 = 32$ for both the top-left and bottom-right blocks), whereas Square~\texttt  {\#599} exhibits severe spatial concentration, with $w_1 = 48$ in the top-left block versus $w_1 = 16$ in the bottom-right block.}}{9}{figure.30}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:window_entropy}{{2}{9}{\textbf {Multiscale sliding-window Shannon entropy, $2\times 2$ quartet energy census, and extreme board textures.} \textbf {(a)} Normalized $\ell _1$ window entropy $\widetilde {H}_1(k)$ versus relative scale $k/n$ across five constructive magic-square families ($n=3$ Lo Shu, $n=4,8$ Doubly-Even, $n=5$ Siamese, and $n=6$ Conway LUX). Dotted vertical drop lines connect $\widetilde {H}_1(2)$ to hollow markers representing the $\ell _2$ window entropy $\widetilde {H}_2(2)$ at $k=2$, which drops sharply to $0.91498$ ($n=4$) and $0.90598$ ($n=8$) due to extreme corner/center magnitude clustering in doubly-even diagonal masks, while odd-order Siamese squares retain high local uniformity ($\widetilde {H}_2(2) \ge 0.94254$). \textbf {(b)} Joint census of interior $2\times 2$ quartet energy $W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm {int}}(S)$ and window entropy $\widetilde {H}_1(2)$ across all $880$ Fr\'enicle order-$4$ magic squares. In accordance with \Cref {lem:quartet_equivalence}, vanishing of interior quartet energy forces vanishing of toroidal quartet energy ($W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm {int}} = W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm {tor}} = 0$, vertical dashed line), uniquely isolating the $48$ panmagic squares of Dudeney Group~I. Extremal boards are highlighted: global maximum entropy Square~\texttt {\#123} ($\widetilde {H}_1(2)=0.99967$, $W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm {int}}=512$, $W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm {tor}}=1{,}024$, magenta star) and global minimum entropy Square~\texttt {\#599} ($\widetilde {H}_1(2)=0.94035$, $W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm {int}}=512$, $W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm {tor}}=1{,}024$, dark red triangle), whereas global interior quartet extrema across the census are realized by Square~\texttt {\#145} ($W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm {int}}=384$) and Square~\texttt {\#219} ($W_{2\times 2}^{\mathrm {int}}=2{,}816$). \textbf {(c1, c2)} Texture heatmaps of $|Z_{ij}|$ for the extremal squares. Square~\texttt {\#123} exhibits perfectly balanced $2\times 2$ $\ell _1$ weights ($w_1 = 32$ for both the top-left and bottom-right blocks), whereas Square~\texttt {\#599} exhibits severe spatial concentration, with $w_1 = 48$ in the top-left block versus $w_1 = 16$ in the bottom-right block}{figure.30}{}}
