\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Exhaustive $S_9$ permutation landscape ($362{,}880$ states) and the $3$-stage combination-lock saddle pathway at order $n=3$.} \textbf  {(a)} Histogram of the centred line Hamiltonian $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}(S) = \mathbf  {z}^\top L_3 \mathbf  {z}$ across all $9! = 362{,}880$ permutations of $S_9$, showing the ensemble mean $\mathbb  {E}[\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}] = 2\|\mathbf  {z}\|^2 = 480$ (orange dashed line) and global maximum $\max \mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}= 720$ (purple dash-dotted line). Inset: Zoom of low-energy levels ($\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}\le 24$), resolving the $8$ Lo Shu ground states at $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}=0$ ($74.53\%$ deterministic steepest-descent basin), the forbidden gap at $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}=4$ ($0$ states), the $8$ strict local-minimum traps $S_{\mathrm  {trap}}^{(3)}$ at $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}=8$ ($25.47\%$ basin), followed by $16$ states at $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}=12$, $0$ at $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}=16$, $48$ at $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}=20$, and $32$ at $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}=24$. \textbf  {(b)} Three-stage combination-lock pathway (\Cref  {thm:s9_traps}) escaping the antipodal trap $S_{\mathrm  {trap}}^{(3)}$: (1) Trap state $S_{\mathrm  {trap}}^{(3)}$ ($\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}=8$), with balanced rows and diagonals but frustrated outer columns ($\Sigma = 14, 15, 16$), where all $36$ single swaps increase energy by $\ge +4$ and all $168$ directed $3$-cycles increase energy by $\ge +8$; (2) Intermediate single-swap saddle $\tau _1 S_{\mathrm  {trap}}^{(3)}$ reached by the intra-row swap $\tau _1 = (6\leftrightarrow 7)$ in Row~1 ($\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}^\ddagger = 12$, activation barrier $\Delta \mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}^\ddagger = +4$, shifting residuals to $C_1=14, C_2=16, D_-=14$); (3) Lo Shu ground state $S_{\mathrm  {LoShu}}$ reached by conjugate intra-row swap $\tau _2 = (3\leftrightarrow 4)$ in Row~3 ($\Delta \mathcal  {H}_2 = -12$, restoring all line sums to $15$). Bottom panel: Potential energy profile $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}$ along the reaction coordinate, demonstrating that line-preserving $(2,2)$ double transpositions expand the deterministic ground-state basin of $S_9$ from $74.53\%$ to $100.00\%$.}}{14}{figure.50}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:s9_landscape}{{4}{14}{\textbf {Exhaustive $S_9$ permutation landscape ($362{,}880$ states) and the $3$-stage combination-lock saddle pathway at order $n=3$.} \textbf {(a)} Histogram of the centred line Hamiltonian $\Hline (S) = \mathbf {z}^\top L_3 \mathbf {z}$ across all $9! = 362{,}880$ permutations of $S_9$, showing the ensemble mean $\mathbb {E}[\Hline ] = 2\|\mathbf {z}\|^2 = 480$ (orange dashed line) and global maximum $\max \Hline = 720$ (purple dash-dotted line). Inset: Zoom of low-energy levels ($\Hline \le 24$), resolving the $8$ Lo Shu ground states at $\Hline =0$ ($74.53\%$ deterministic steepest-descent basin), the forbidden gap at $\Hline =4$ ($0$ states), the $8$ strict local-minimum traps $S_{\mathrm {trap}}^{(3)}$ at $\Hline =8$ ($25.47\%$ basin), followed by $16$ states at $\Hline =12$, $0$ at $\Hline =16$, $48$ at $\Hline =20$, and $32$ at $\Hline =24$. \textbf {(b)} Three-stage combination-lock pathway (\Cref {thm:s9_traps}) escaping the antipodal trap $S_{\mathrm {trap}}^{(3)}$: (1) Trap state $S_{\mathrm {trap}}^{(3)}$ ($\Hline =8$), with balanced rows and diagonals but frustrated outer columns ($\Sigma = 14, 15, 16$), where all $36$ single swaps increase energy by $\ge +4$ and all $168$ directed $3$-cycles increase energy by $\ge +8$; (2) Intermediate single-swap saddle $\tau _1 S_{\mathrm {trap}}^{(3)}$ reached by the intra-row swap $\tau _1 = (6\leftrightarrow 7)$ in Row~1 ($\Hline ^\ddagger = 12$, activation barrier $\Delta \Hline ^\ddagger = +4$, shifting residuals to $C_1=14, C_2=16, D_-=14$); (3) Lo Shu ground state $S_{\mathrm {LoShu}}$ reached by conjugate intra-row swap $\tau _2 = (3\leftrightarrow 4)$ in Row~3 ($\Delta \mathcal {H}_2 = -12$, restoring all line sums to $15$). Bottom panel: Potential energy profile $\Hline $ along the reaction coordinate, demonstrating that line-preserving $(2,2)$ double transpositions expand the deterministic ground-state basin of $S_9$ from $74.53\%$ to $100.00\%$}{figure.50}{}}
