\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Order-$4$ ($S_{16}$) steepest-descent relaxation envelopes and combinatorial $(2,2)$ plaquette escape census ($2{,}000$ uniform random starts).} \textbf  {(a)} Steepest-descent relaxation envelopes ($20\%\text  {--}80\%$ interdecile bands) and six representative trajectories of shifted line energy $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}(S_t) + 4$ (log scale) versus transposition step $t$. Pure $2$-cycle steepest descent halts in frustrated local minima ($\Delta \mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}> 0$) in $81.75\%$ of trials ($1{,}635/2{,}000$, orange), concentrating heavily in the dominant frustration band $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}\in \{8, 12, 16\}$ (shaded yellow). Only $18.25\%$ ($365/2{,}000$, green) reach the magic ground state $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}=0$ directly (dashed green line), halting after a mean of $8.18$ steps. \textbf  {(b)} Terminal local-minimum spectrum $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}(S_\infty )$ across all $2{,}000$ trials (solid bars), overlaid with the yield unlocked by a single line-preserving $(2,2)$ plaquette move (hatched blue bars). The frustration band $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}\in \{8, 12, 16\}$ accounts for $57.1\%$ ($1{,}142/2{,}000$) of all starts ($470$ at $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}=8$, $305$ at $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}=12$, $367$ at $\mathcal  {H}_{\mathrm  {line}}=16$). Testing line-preserving $(2,2)$ double swaps unlocks $16.57\%$ ($271/1{,}635$) of the trapped minima ($4.8\times $ more than directed $3$-cycles, which escape only $3.43\%$), lifting deterministic zero-temperature ground-state convergence from $18.25\%$ ($365/2{,}000$) to $25.45\%$ ($509/2{,}000$).}}{16}{figure.57}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:s16_descent}{{5}{16}{\textbf {Order-$4$ ($S_{16}$) steepest-descent relaxation envelopes and combinatorial $(2,2)$ plaquette escape census ($2{,}000$ uniform random starts).} \textbf {(a)} Steepest-descent relaxation envelopes ($20\%\text {--}80\%$ interdecile bands) and six representative trajectories of shifted line energy $\Hline (S_t) + 4$ (log scale) versus transposition step $t$. Pure $2$-cycle steepest descent halts in frustrated local minima ($\Delta \Hline > 0$) in $81.75\%$ of trials ($1{,}635/2{,}000$, orange), concentrating heavily in the dominant frustration band $\Hline \in \{8, 12, 16\}$ (shaded yellow). Only $18.25\%$ ($365/2{,}000$, green) reach the magic ground state $\Hline =0$ directly (dashed green line), halting after a mean of $8.18$ steps. \textbf {(b)} Terminal local-minimum spectrum $\Hline (S_\infty )$ across all $2{,}000$ trials (solid bars), overlaid with the yield unlocked by a single line-preserving $(2,2)$ plaquette move (hatched blue bars). The frustration band $\Hline \in \{8, 12, 16\}$ accounts for $57.1\%$ ($1{,}142/2{,}000$) of all starts ($470$ at $\Hline =8$, $305$ at $\Hline =12$, $367$ at $\Hline =16$). Testing line-preserving $(2,2)$ double swaps unlocks $16.57\%$ ($271/1{,}635$) of the trapped minima ($4.8\times $ more than directed $3$-cycles, which escape only $3.43\%$), lifting deterministic zero-temperature ground-state convergence from $18.25\%$ ($365/2{,}000$) to $25.45\%$ ($509/2{,}000$)}{figure.57}{}}
